        "title": "Air Masses and Fronts - Classification, Frontal Theory, Norwegian Cyclone Model",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "An air mass is a large body of air with horizontally uniform temperature and humidity, acquired by sitting over a source region. Fronts are the narrow boundaries between contrasting air masses. The Norwegian cyclone model (Bjerknes et al., 1918–1920) describes how extratropical cyclones develop along the polar front — still the conceptual foundation of synoptic forecasting."
